# Resume & Bio-data Website

A multi-page personal website containing a **Resume** and **Bio-data**, built for a Web Technology assignment using HTML, CSS, JavaScript and jQuery, and hosted on GitHub Pages.

**Live site:** https://tanushreehatti.github.io/resume-site/

## About

This website presents the resume and personal details of **Tanushree Hatti**, a Computer Science and Engineering student at RV Institute of Technology and Management, Bangalore (2024-2028). The design follows a developer theme, with a code-editor style hero section and an interactive terminal on the home page.

## Pages

| Page | File | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| Home | `index.html` | Intro, code-style profile card, interactive terminal, stats and education timeline |
| Resume | `resume.html` | Skills, objective, education, projects and research papers, with a print-ready PDF layout |
| Projects | `projects.html` | Project cards with category filters |
| Bio-data | `biodata.html` | Personal details in a table |
| Contact | `contact.html` | Contact details and a validated contact form |

## Features

- Multi-page layout with a shared responsive navigation bar and mobile menu
- Dark and light theme toggle, saved in the browser
- Typing animation and animated counters on the home page
- Interactive terminal (`about`, `skills`, `projects`, `education`, `contact`, `theme`, `clear`)
- Scroll progress bar, fade-in on scroll and back-to-top button
- Project filtering with jQuery
- Contact form validation (name, email format, message length)
- "Download as PDF" button with a dedicated print stylesheet (one-page A4 resume)
- Responsive design for desktop, tablet and mobile

## Technologies Used

- **HTML5**: semantic elements (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`, `aside`, `table`, `form`, `footer`)
- **CSS3**: variables, flexbox, grid, animations, media queries, print stylesheet
- **JavaScript and jQuery 3.7.1**: DOM manipulation, events, animations, form validation, local storage
- **Google Fonts**: Inter and JetBrains Mono
- **Git and GitHub Pages**: version control and hosting

## Project Structure

```
resume-site/
├── index.html
├── resume.html
├── projects.html
├── biodata.html
├── contact.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
└── README.md
```

## Run Locally

1. Clone the repository:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/tanushreehatti/resume-site.git
   ```
2. Open the folder in VS Code.
3. Right-click `index.html` and choose **Open with Live Server** (or simply open `index.html` in a browser).

## Deployment

The site is deployed with GitHub Pages:

1. Push the code to the `main` branch.
2. Go to **Settings -> Pages**.
3. Select **Deploy from a branch**, choose `main` and `/ (root)`, then save.

